=Write the body content for one section of a blog post.

Article title: {{ $('Normalize Outline Data').first().json.page_title }}
Target keywords: {{ $('Set Article Parameters').first().json.keywords }}
Target audience: {{ $('Set Article Parameters').first().json.target_audience }}
Tone of voice: {{ $('Set Article Parameters').first().json.tone_of_voice }}

Section heading (H2): {{ $json.title }}
Section brief: {{ $json.chapter_prompt }}

Content rules:
- Cover only this section's heading and brief.
- Open with a clear first paragraph that answers or frames the question in the heading.
- Reflect the reader's perspective naturally and explain why the topic matters in practical terms.
- Use the target keywords only where they fit naturally.
- Do not write an overall article introduction or a conclusion.
- Do not repeat the heading and do not add any headings.
- Aim for about {{ Math.max(80, Math.round(($('Set Article Parameters').first().json.max_words - 100) / $('Normalize Outline Data').first().json.headings.length)) }} words.

Formatting rules:
- Return only HTML. No markdown, no code fences, no explanation.
- Wrap every paragraph in <p> tags.
- Allowed tags: <p>, <b>, <i>, <ul>, <ol>, <li>.

